  "query_preview": "..An upper-level cutoff low digging southward into\nArizona this evening will continue to bring gusty northerly winds\nto portions of southwestern Utah tonight. Main area of concern is \naround the Pine Valley mountains and through Black Ridge Canyon, \nwhere gusts 30-40 mph are expected through early Saturday morning.\nOtherwise, quiescent conditions remain in place across the\nremainder of the region.\n\nLongwave ridging is expected to strengthen in the wake of this \nexiting low this weekend into next week, allowing dry conditions \nto continue with a gradual warming trend. As we're heading into\nthe cool season, this persistent ridging resulting in warming \ntemperatures aloft will be favorable for strengthening valley\ninversions, leading to some developing haze into next week.\nEnsembles still support a weak shortwave to graze northern Utah\nlate Tuesday, though little impact is expected to the area outside\nof slight cooling mid-week and potential to mix out some of the\nhaze building up across inverted valleys. Behind this wave,\nridging redevelops across the west, amplifying in response to a\ndeepening longwave trough off the west coast. \n\nLong-range guidance does indicate a shift in the pattern by late\nnext week as the aforementioned trough moves inland, favoring a\ncooler and wetter pattern across the west into next weekend.",
